@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix st: <https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/structure#> .

<https://hexplain.io/ns/aspect/structure> skos:scopeNote "Use for decoded records, member roles and ordered occurrences when a more specific domain aspect does not supply those meanings. Physical byte layout remains in BDDO; format profiles supply application-specific member semantics."@en .
st:CountShape rdfs:label "Count Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using st:byteCount, st:count, st:elementCount. A described value has at most one st:byteCount, an integer within the xsd:unsignedLong value space (rdfs:range xsd:unsignedLong). A described value has at most one st:count, a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). A described value has at most one st:elementCount, an integer within the xsd:unsignedLong value space (rdfs:range xsd:unsignedLong)."@en .
st:IntegerValueShape skos:definition "Applied through references from other shapes. An integer value is a literal of an XSD integer-family datatype (xsd:integer, xsd:positiveInteger, xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:int, xsd:long, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:short, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:byte or xsd:unsignedByte). A conforming value is an integer (of any XSD integer datatype)."@en .
st:Item skos:definition "One occurrence in an ordered collection; its instance path identifies its sequence position."@en .
st:Member skos:definition "One identified component of a record, related to its name, optional numeric identifier and decoded value."@en .
st:MemberShape rdfs:label "Member Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to instances of st:Member; subjects using st:name. A record member has exactly one st:name."@en .
st:RangeDatatypeShape skos:definition "Applies to subjects using st:dataType, st:identifier, st:name, st:recordType, st:symbol. st:dataType takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). st:identifier takes an integer (rdfs:range xsd:integer). st:name takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). st:recordType takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). st:symbol takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string)."@en .
st:Record skos:definition "A structured decoded value whose member identities and value interpretations are specified by a format description."@en .
st:SingleValueShape rdfs:label "Single Value Shape"@en ;
    skos:definition "Applies to subjects using st:identifier, st:value. A member, item or record has at most one st:identifier. A member, item or record has at most one st:value."@en .
st:count skos:definition "A non-negative count associated with a described value, in a unit (elements or bytes) its source profile fixes; the general form of st:elementCount and st:byteCount."@en .
st:dataType skos:definition "The textual type or interpretation label assigned to a decoded value."@en .
st:elementCount skos:definition "The number of elements a described collection or value holds, including zero for an empty one."@en .
st:hasItem skos:definition "Relates a collection-bearing value to an individually described element occurrence."@en .
st:hasMember skos:definition "Relates a record to one component whose name or identifier distinguishes its role."@en .
st:identifier skos:definition "The integer code identifying a component or occurrence in the representation described by its profile."@en .
st:name skos:definition "The decoded textual name identifying a record component in its containing record."@en .
st:recordType skos:definition "The declared record-kind name supplied by the describing schema or interface definition."@en .
st:symbol skos:definition "The symbolic name associated with a declared enumeration code."@en .
st:value skos:definition "The interpreted scalar literal or structured resource carried by a member, item or record."@en .
